    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>Improve the UX by adding a UR selector in the UI of your site!</p>\n<p>This plugins provides a set of tools in order to let visitors select a <em>profile</em> and have filtered content during the visit.</p>\n<p>You can add as many personas as you want, assign posts the them and display a customizable selector on your site.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload <code>personalizer</code> to the <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code> directory</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the &#8216;Plugins&#8217; menu in WordPress admin</li>\n<li>Go to the settings page in Settings &gt; PersonaLizer</li>\n<li>Check the post-types you want to be filtered</li>\n<li>In any submenu of selected post-types (eg: posts), access to the Persona manager, and add some ones</li>\n<li>Assign posts to personas</li>\n<li>Add the persona selector on front with the provided block</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "changelog": "<h3>1.0.0</h3>\n<p>Initial release</p>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Improve the UX by adding a UR selector in the UI of your site! Persona selection and filtering.",
    "description": "<p>Improve the UX by adding a UR selector in the UI of your site!</p>\n<p>This plugins provides a set of tools in order to let visitors select a <em>profile</em> and have filtered content during the visit.</p>\n<p>You can add as many personas as you want, assign posts the them and display a customizable selector on your site.</p>\n",
